'' '?' IS PRINT, and keeping TK_QUESTION in the statement's 'op' made a second
'' statement KIND out of a pure synonym. The lowerer dispatches on the op, so every '?'
'' reached the end of the dispatcher and declined while the 'print' beside it lowered.
''
'' Recorded as KW_PRINT in the parser rather than dispatched twice in lowering: the
'' two are the same statement, and every later pass that reads the op -- the lowerer,
'' the statistics, a future diagnostic -- would otherwise each need to know about both.
''
'' syntax/non-indexed-array.bas writes it.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/question-print.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: bound.hit
'' GOLDEN: expected/question-print.out
